## Rules of the road

- **Tests ship with features.** Every change to behavior lands with tests in the same commit.
- **Changelog entries ship with changes people notice.** Any `feat`, `fix` or `perf` commit adds a line under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md`. CI checks this on PRs.
- **One concern per PR.** Split unrelated changes.

## Commit style

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org) with Title-Case scopes: `feat(Engine): add a tone control`. Keep the subject under about 50 characters, and use the body to explain why.

## Releases

The maintainer runs `scripts/release`, which works out the version from the commits, tags it and pushes. CI builds and publishes from the tag.
